<PageLayout title="How TotalRecalls Works — 5 Simple Steps" description="Learn how TotalRecalls downloads and indexes your AI chat history to local Markdown and JSON files on your PC in 5 simple, private steps." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "How It Works" }]}>
  <h1>How It Works</h1>
  <p>TotalRecalls saves your AI conversations into a private folder on your computer — readable Markdown + JSON you keep forever. Five steps from scattered chats to one local folder.</p>

  <section class="how-it-works">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li><span class="step-icon">1</span><span><strong>Buy once</strong> — checkout via Paddle. One-time $24<span class="tr-usd">USD</span> launch price, no subscription. Your license key arrives by email immediately — enter it in the app to unlock all 8 providers.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-icon">2</span><span><strong>Install</strong> — install from the Microsoft Store or unzip and run TotalRecalls.exe. No background services, no account. Windows 10/11.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-icon">3</span><span><strong>Pick a provider</strong> — ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini (via Google Takeout), Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, or Qwen Chat. You sign in locally, exactly like a browser.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-icon">4</span><span><strong>Download</strong> — conversations land in a Library folder on your PC as Markdown + JSON, organized per provider. Browse, search, or back them up anywhere.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-icon">5</span><span><strong>Search &amp; Ask</strong> — browse in File Explorer, Obsidian, or Notion, or launch the Smart Search Engine (SSE) add-on to search and chat across all 8 providers in plain English.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Everything stays on your machine — a plain folder of files you own.</li>
      <li>Session tokens are used locally and never leave your PC.</li>
      <li>No cloud locker. No TotalRecalls account. Nothing to sign up for.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you get per provider</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>ChatGPT</strong> — every conversation as Markdown + JSON, including images and metadata. See the <a href="/guides/export-chatgpt-conversations/">ChatGPT download guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Claude</strong> — Projects and long conversations, kept as files. See the <a href="/guides/export-claude-chat-history/">Claude download guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Perplexity</strong> — research conversations before you lose the tab trail. See the <a href="/guides/export-perplexity-conversations/">Perplexity download guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Gemini</strong> — uses your Google Takeout folder/JSON (the most reliable path). See the <a href="/guides/gemini-takeout-archive/">Gemini Takeout guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Grok</strong> — session scanning on grok.com. See the <a href="/guides/grok/">Grok download guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>DeepSeek</strong> — downloads from chat.deepseek.com, with chain-of-thought blocks preserved. See the <a href="/guides/deepseek/">DeepSeek download guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Mistral</strong> — downloads from chat.mistral.ai (Le Chat). See the <a href="/guides/mistral/">Mistral download guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Qwen Chat</strong> — downloads from chat.qwen.ai (the consumer product; DashScope developer APIs are not used). See the <a href="/guides/qwen/">Qwen download guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Will my provider block me?</strong> TotalRecalls works within each provider's own download/Takeout features — you must follow their terms.</li>
      <li><strong>Mac?</strong> Windows today (WebView2). Mac is planned if demand is real.</li>
      <li><strong>Will Windows warn me?</strong> No. TotalRecalls is certified and distributed through the Microsoft Store, so installation is one-click with no security warnings.</li>
      <li>More answers in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

